{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And a man's hallowed things shall be his.</b> But the rest of the hallowed things — terumot and tithot — even though they are consecrated to HaShem, do not belong to any particular priest, but to whichever priest the owners give them to." "<b>Whatsoever any man gives to the priest.</b> But when one of the owners gives some hallowed thing to a priest, it no longer falls under 'his hallowed things,' but it shall belong to the priest who receives it, and neither the owners nor any other priests can take it from him."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:04.951763471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}